{"parentUuid":"d264905a-b26f-4075-9bf1-3aafab995d71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfBCC21meR4JgHbQUJNGy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DnkawW2uqVrC3t5sJAfa6W","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i '/monkeypatch.setattr(lotka_module.plt, \"subplots\", plt.subplots)/d' tests/test_lotka.py && cat > bugfix-plan.md <<'E'\n# Bugfix plan: CLI passes gamma as delta\n\n## Problem\n`lotka` CLI produces wrong trajectories (bug_ticket/issue.md). The library solver is correct.\n\n## Red evidence\n- `solve_lotkavolterra(1.0, 0.1, 1.5, 0.075, 10, 5, 40, 100)` matches `bug_ticket/lotka_correct_trajectory.csv` exactly (max abs diff 0.0 for x and y).\n- With delta=1.5 (gamma's value) the diff is 40.6 (x) / 135.6 (y).\n- New regression test `tests/test_lotka.py::test_cli_passes_delta_argument_to_solver` fails: `assert 1.5 == 0.075`.\n  Command: `python3 -m pytest tests/test_lotka.py -q`\n\n## Culprit\n`src/qa/lotka.py`, `main()`: `delta=args.gamma` in the `solve_lotkavolterra(...)` call; `--delta` is parsed but never used.\nThe existing CLI test mocks the solver and never asserted on its kwargs, so it missed this.\n\n## Fix\nChange `delta=args.gamma` to `delta=args.delta`. One line.\n\n## Tests\nAdd the regression test above (already added; asserts delta and gamma reach the solver).\n\n## Proof\nRegression test passes; full `tests/test_lotka.py` with line+branch coverage.\n\n## Risks / rollback\nMinimal; only affects CLI argument wiring. Revert the one-line change.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1280,"cache_read_input_tokens":57839,"output_tokens":703,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":44},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1280,"ephemeral_5m_